{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00559",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.59,
      "end_seconds": 11.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.78,
      "text": "Good morning. You are Kavitha Raman, yes? Please tell me if I am saying your name wrongly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.15,
      "end_seconds": 16.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "No, no, it is correct, doctor. Kavitha Raman."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.63,
      "end_seconds": 24.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "Lovely. Please sit, Kavitha. Tell me, what is troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.06,
      "end_seconds": 34.58,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "It is... there is a swelling in my neck. I noticed, um... actually my sister noticed it first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.57,
      "end_seconds": 43.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "A swelling in your neck, and your sister saw it first. When was that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.1,
      "end_seconds": 58.31,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "Three months back, maybe. In a photo. She said, 'what is that', and then I..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.19,
      "end_seconds": 66.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Take your time. And since then, has it changed, bigger, smaller, same?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.45,
      "end_seconds": 76.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "A little bigger, I think. Or maybe I am only looking at it more now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.93,
      "end_seconds": 85.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "That is fair. Does it cause any trouble when you are eating or drinking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.4,
      "end_seconds": 96.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.03,
      "text": "Sometimes food gets stuck. Especially rice, if I eat fast. Then I drink water and it goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.44,
      "end_seconds": 106.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "So food gets stuck sometimes, mostly when you eat fast. Is the swelling painful?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.32,
      "end_seconds": 109.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "No. No pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.78,
      "end_seconds": 117.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "Any difficulty in breathing, even when you lie down at night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.88,
      "end_seconds": 121.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "No, breathing is okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.95,
      "end_seconds": 128.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "And your voice, has it become hoarse or different?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.34,
      "end_seconds": 132.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "No... same only."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.21,
      "end_seconds": 139.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "Good. Anything else you have noticed, anything at all? Even something small."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.85,
      "end_seconds": 149.14,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "I am feeling very tired, doctor. Mostly in the evenings. I thought it is work."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.76,
      "end_seconds": 159.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Very tired in the evenings. Thank you for telling me. Any other health condition, anything you are known for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.69,
      "end_seconds": 163.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Only PCOS. Since college days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.42,
      "end_seconds": 174.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "PCOS, okay. What work do you do, and how is your food, vegetarian or not?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.26,
      "end_seconds": 181.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "I work in a bank. Vegetarian, mostly. Sometimes egg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.03,
      "end_seconds": 197.38,
      "duration_seconds": 13.35,
      "text": "Okay. Now I will examine your neck. Please take a sip of water, hold it in your mouth, and swallow when I say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.69,
      "end_seconds": 200.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.28,
      "end_seconds": 219.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Yes, now swallow. And again. One more time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.34,
      "end_seconds": 230.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.8,
      "text": "Your thyroid gland is enlarged, Kavitha, and it moves up when you swallow. It feels smooth and even."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.91,
      "end_seconds": 237.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Doctor, is it... is it something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.52,
      "end_seconds": 257.6,
      "duration_seconds": 18.08,
      "text": "Let me tell you what I found, so we are both clear. A swelling for three months, no pain, food sticking sometimes, and a smooth enlarged gland. This looks like a goitre, which means an enlarged thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.38,
      "end_seconds": 264.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Goitre. I have never heard this word before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.76,
      "end_seconds": 284.79,
      "duration_seconds": 18.03,
      "text": "It is a common word for it, so please do not worry. First we need to know how your thyroid is working, so I would like a thyroid blood test today itself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.31,
      "end_seconds": 289.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Today? Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 291.93,
      "end_seconds": 299.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "Doctor, shall I take her to the sample room? The phlebotomist is free now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.54,
      "end_seconds": 310.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "Yes, please, Meena. Kavitha, Meena will take your blood. It is a small prick, nothing more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.31,
      "end_seconds": 317.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Okay. And after that I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.27,
      "end_seconds": 332.27,
      "duration_seconds": 13.0,
      "text": "Yes. Go home, eat normally and rest. And remember, if the swelling grows quickly, or the swallowing becomes worse, come back to me straightaway."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.5,
      "end_seconds": 337.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Straightaway. Yes, I will remember."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.05,
      "end_seconds": 350.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.52,
      "text": "Good. So the plan is a blood test today, and coming back quickly if it grows or swallowing worsens. You have done well, Kavitha."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.0,
      "end_seconds": 357.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I was very afraid to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.78,
      "end_seconds": 362.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Many people are. Go with Meena now."
    }
  ]
}
